{
  "hadith_number": 18,
  "text": "On the authority of Abu Dhajjundub Ibn Jnada, an Abu Abdahman Muad Ibn Jabbal, May Allah be pleased of him both, that the messenger of Allah, made a blessings and peace of Allah be upon him, said, Fahya Allah, wherever you are, and follow up, a bad deed with a good one, and it will wipe it out, and behave well towards people. It was related by a timid he, who said it was a good head-deaf, and in some copies of a timid he's collection, it will said to be a good and signed head-deaf.",
